(6837672, 1028210, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bassbone:</b></div><hr/><i> very nicely composed - i almost wish there was a subject on the street to make the scene more alive. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yeah it does feel like it is missing something. A nice vintage car or horse and cart would do it though more likely to be a caravan or motorhome passing by:)</td>', 'Originally posted by bassbone: very nicely composed - i almost wish there was a subject on the street to make the scene more alive.  Yeah it does feel like it is missing something. A nice vintage car or horse and cart would do it though more likely to be a caravan or motorhome passing by:)', '2012-08-08 06:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6837674, 1027999, 108580, '<td valign="top">Despite some dust cloning, crop, slight sat increase my entry this FS was also untouched. Judging by some responses to it and previous FS work submitted I have come to learn that if it isn''t made ''unreal'', change bland grey water to fusion dayglo blue water (the way water should be right?), that is nothing like it was to my naked eye at time of shot, it won''t fare better scorewise...pfffffft. Enough voters this time appreciated it.</td>', 'Despite some dust cloning, crop, slight sat increase my entry this FS was also untouched. Judging by some responses to it and previous FS work submitted I have come to learn that if it isn''t made ''unreal'', change bland grey water to fusion dayglo blue water (the way water should be right?), that is nothing like it was to my naked eye at time of shot, it won''t fare better scorewise...pfffffft. Enough voters this time appreciated it.', '2012-08-08 07:07:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6837675, 1026969, 103032, '<td valign="top">I neglected to comment on this.  I really liked the "pattern" and "texture" created by the rocks.  I initially didn''t catch the boy in my first second of looking.  I think that''s why I liked this so much; the kid is camouflaged.  Great shot.  FWIW, I was one of your 8''s.</td>', 'I neglected to comment on this.  I really liked the "pattern" and "texture" created by the rocks.  I initially didn''t catch the boy in my first second of looking.  I think that''s why I liked this so much; the kid is camouflaged.  Great shot.  FWIW, I was one of your 8''s.', '2012-08-08 07:23:57.000000', NULL, 0),
