(6857625, 1026760, 60862, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot.  Congrats on the ribbon!<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Venser:</b></div><hr/><i> Holy shit, I''m sorry. <br/>I thought I was bumping this up at the last minute from a 9 to a 10, instead I''m your 1 vote. In every free study I always choose one photo to be the best of the lot, and this was it, at least in theory. Turns out I placed you at the bottom with the chafe. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ll let you off the hook.  If your 1 had instead been a 10, it would''ve raised the score to 7.2149, still in 3rd place.</td>', 'Awesome shot.  Congrats on the ribbon! Originally posted by Venser: Holy shit, I''m sorry. I thought I was bumping this up at the last minute from a 9 to a 10, instead I''m your 1 vote. In every free study I always choose one photo to be the best of the lot, and this was it, at least in theory. Turns out I placed you at the bottom with the chafe.   I''ll let you off the hook.  If your 1 had instead been a 10, it would''ve raised the score to 7.2149, still in 3rd place.', '2012-09-05 23:28:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6857823, 1026760, 81042, '<td valign="top">Friends, Thanks for the many kind comments. Africa is so full of amazing life.<br/> <br/>Sorry for my slowness in responding, our family is in the midst of moving to Kenya and life has been somewhat hectic. <br/> <br/>Venser - no sweat on the 1. Appreciate you letting me know. Mistakes happen, at least I seem to make them all the time :) <br/> <br/>Levyj413 thanks for answering on my behalf :) - when I saw your reply I thought - "crap I should have done that earlier" but have been slow when I should have made it a priority. <br/> <br/>Love the DPC community!</td>', 'Friends, Thanks for the many kind comments. Africa is so full of amazing life. Sorry for my slowness in responding, our family is in the midst of moving to Kenya and life has been somewhat hectic.  Venser - no sweat on the 1. Appreciate you letting me know. Mistakes happen, at least I seem to make them all the time :)  Levyj413 thanks for answering on my behalf :) - when I saw your reply I thought - "crap I should have done that earlier" but have been slow when I should have made it a priority.  Love the DPC community!', '2012-09-06 04:46:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(6858703, 1027234, 59029, '<td valign="top">Great lighting and subject, I just wish there weren''t so much white flanking her and a little more headroom... in other words more of a portrait crop than a landscape.  Also the darker arm on the left is a little offputting, looks dirty, just draws my eye in the wrong way.  Hope this helps!</td>', 'Great lighting and subject, I just wish there weren''t so much white flanking her and a little more headroom... in other words more of a portrait crop than a landscape.  Also the darker arm on the left is a little offputting, looks dirty, just draws my eye in the wrong way.  Hope this helps!', '2012-09-06 22:49:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6858706, 1027234, 67697, '<td valign="top">I gave it a 7 because I liked the processing and I thought her gaze was intriguing.</td>', 'I gave it a 7 because I liked the processing and I thought her gaze was intriguing.', '2012-09-06 22:53:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6858709, 1027234, 42256, '<td valign="top">Beautifully lit, catch light in her eye is just right, color tones and temperature work well, no blown highlights with a while background is a big plus - well sharpened. I gave this a 6 during voting. <br/> <br/>A different crop (closer, portrait orientation, cropped till her tattoo) might have worked better imo.</td>', 'Beautifully lit, catch light in her eye is just right, color tones and temperature work well, no blown highlights with a while background is a big plus - well sharpened. I gave this a 6 during voting.  A different crop (closer, portrait orientation, cropped till her tattoo) might have worked better imo.', '2012-09-06 22:57:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6859373, 1027234, 101702, '<td valign="top">Commenting for the critique thread - somehow I missed this at voting time, I think I was taking a break from voting at the time. I would have scored this a 7-8 depending on the strength of the competition in the free study.<br/> <br/>I''m really just echoing other commenters now - for me the amount of white is overwhelming and a portrait crop might help with that or just an off centre composition. I also agree that the right arm looks a bit dirty, but not enough for me to mark down. <br/> <br/>Other than that, the clarity and processing are spot on. What keeps this from being in the 9-10 range for me is that extra spark of something ''different'' and little (picky) things like the crumpling of her dress around her right breast, her hair obscuring the necklace and suchlike which just feel like a lack of ''polish''. Of course, with her tattoos, piercings, and hair colours, she probably wouldn''t suit being so perfectly polished.<br/> <br/>I think the 1-4 marks you got were uncalled for, but it''s the large amount of 5''s that probably did you. I''m not getting why this would be a 5 (i.e. below average) - completely disagree with that.<br/> <br/>On the whole a very good image, but with room for improvement.<br/></td>', 'Commenting for the critique thread - somehow I missed this at voting time, I think I was taking a break from voting at the time. I would have scored this a 7-8 depending on the strength of the competition in the free study. I''m really just echoing other commenters now - for me the amount of white is overwhelming and a portrait crop might help with that or just an off centre composition. I also agree that the right arm looks a bit dirty, but not enough for me to mark down.  Other than that, the clarity and processing are spot on. What keeps this from being in the 9-10 range for me is that extra spark of something ''different'' and little (picky) things like the crumpling of her dress around her right breast, her hair obscuring the necklace and suchlike which just feel like a lack of ''polish''. Of course, with her tattoos, piercings, and hair colours, she probably wouldn''t suit being so perfectly polished. I think the 1-4 marks you got were uncalled for, but it''s the large amount of 5''s that probably did you. I''m not getting why this would be a 5 (i.e. below average) - completely disagree with that. On the whole a very good image, but with room for improvement.', '2012-09-07 14:28:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6859564, 1028006, 83313, '<td valign="top">Not unlike the performance of many of my own cycling related shots. My cycling friends think they are great and wow over them, but DPC greets them with a big fat "MEH". But then, our cycling buddies are not impressed by the ability to ride 40 miles. That''s an average morning ride. Our photography friends think 40 miles is an unbelievable distance and that we are insane. <br/> <br/>It''s all relative.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-09-07 16:50:33.</i></td>', 'Not unlike the performance of many of my own cycling related shots. My cycling friends think they are great and wow over them, but DPC greets them with a big fat "MEH". But then, our cycling buddies are not impressed by the ability to ride 40 miles. That''s an average morning ride. Our photography friends think 40 miles is an unbelievable distance and that we are insane.  It''s all relative.', '2012-09-07 17:49:52.000000', '2012-09-07 17:50:33.000000', 0),
